E62 dm-all decision engine image (REAX engine track v2, SN92): one image, one engine per model, chosen by REAX_MODEL.
Our own server code (Apache-2.0) around the stock vLLM 0.30.0 image (Apache-2.0, vLLM contributors).

/opt/blink  (slot blink, Blink v0.3 26B-A4B NVFP4 text): our engine. blink_gemm.cu, blink_moegemm.cu and
            blink_rgemm.cu (ours, Apache-2.0) are compiled against NVIDIA CUTLASS headers (BSD-3-Clause, NVIDIA
            Corporation) shipped in the vLLM image. blink_actq.cu (ours, Apache-2.0) contains device functions
            copied from vLLM 0.30.0 (csrc/libtorch_stable/activation_kernels.cu and quantization/fp4/
            nvfp4_utils.cuh, nvfp4_experts_quant.cu; Apache-2.0, the vLLM contributors and NVIDIA CORPORATION).
            blink_read.py calls vLLM's own sampler kernels. No REAX Engine code.
/opt/jeffan (slot jeffan, Jeffan-31b-1710): our engine; the prompt renderer is the checkpoint's own (read from /model
            at start). No REAX Engine code.
/opt/vision (Blink vision engine, not declared by this image): see /opt/vision/NOTICE. Its patch_vllm.py applies the
            same Gemma4 vision-encoder budget change as the REAX v2 vision reference image (engine/vision_budget.py of
            reax-engine, REAX Engine License 1.1: MIT with one condition; SN92 mining exempt; Copyright 2026
            productivity-boost.com Betriebs UG (haftungsbeschraenkt) & Co. KG, Passau, Germany); the patched
            vllm/model_executor/models/gemma4_mm.py changes behaviour only when REAX_VISION_ENCODER_BUDGET=total10
            (set for the vision engine only). vfuse.py reproduces operations of Hugging Face transformers' Gemma4
            modeling code (Apache-2.0, The HuggingFace Team).
The decision prompt and readout of the Blink engines follow the Blink / Rune "decisions v1" protocol as the reference
serves it.
Kernel configuration tables (pins.json, pins_rms.json, pins_f4.json, bi_tiles.json, moe_gemm.json, rtr_gemm.json, alt/*.json,
gemm_table.json) are tile / launch
configurations of compiled kernels: no weights, scales or calibration statistics. Every tensor is derived at start
from the read-only weights at /model.
