/opt/jeffan (v1x): E73 (pjs) levers on the Jeffan engine. SA, step alignment (JEF_STEP_ALIGN=512,640,768,896,1024;
            merge_align.py edit of jef_levers.py): when at least 3 requests and between 512 tokens and the step budget of
            new tokens are pending (prefix-cache hits excluded), that step's token budget is the largest listed FULL CUDA-graph
            size not above them, so the step runs its graph without padding rows; the rest of the last read is chunked
            into the next step by vLLM's chunked prefill, as SB does at the budget. The budget is restored right after
            scheduling, so the BF wait still tests JEF_STEP_TOK. Scheduling only: the same bits (batch-invariant kernels;
            a chunked read's earlier K/V are read back from the FP8 cache exactly as written; reads stay below the
            1,024-token sliding window). LLP, last-layer row pruning (JEF_LLP, jef_e73lev.py, merge_llp.py) and LLPA
